IMPORT prelude

-- Foreshores Act 1920 (Singapore) -- who must approve a reclamation (s 4(2)), the effect of declaring reclaimed land State land
-- (s 5), the bar on compensation for works and the appeal to the Minister (ss 6, 7), validation of pre-1901 grants (s 8), leases of
-- foreshore and seabed (s 9), temporary occupation licences (s 10), and the farming of beaches and what a farmer may charge (s 11).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FA1920.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amending Act in its
-- Legislative History is Act 16 of 2016 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2016, s 8, from 10 June 2016), which repealed s 3.
-- The SSO metadata beside it reads "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". Section numbers follow the BODY: the arrangement at the top
-- of the deposit is out of step by one (it lists "1." with no heading and puts every heading against the next number).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0153 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (12 sections), so nearly all of it is here. Not encoded: s 1 (short title), s 2 beyond the
-- definitions used, s 3 (repealed), the Government's works powers in s 4(1) except as the source of "the works", s 12 (saving of
-- Government powers and of lessee-sublessee rights) except as a comment, and anything in the State Lands Act 1920 to which ss 5(2)
-- and 10(2) refer (it was not read).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Foreshores Act 1920 -- foreshore and seabed`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `4(2) -- who must approve a reclamation`

-- s 4(2): "The Government may, subject to the approval of Parliament, reclaim any part of the foreshore or seabed of Singapore:
-- Provided that where the part of foreshore or seabed to be reclaimed does not exceed 8 hectares or, if the whole of that part is
-- within port limits, 4 hectares, the approval of Parliament shall not be required and the Minister may authorise such reclamation."
--
-- The smaller ceiling applies only where the WHOLE of the part is within port limits. A 6-hectare reclamation straddling the port
-- limit goes to the Minister; the same 6 hectares wholly inside the port needs Parliament.
DECLARE Approver IS ONE OF
    Parliament
    `the Minister`

GIVEN `wholly within port limits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the ceiling for ministerial authorisation` MEANS
    IF `wholly within port limits` THEN 4 ELSE 8

GIVEN `hectares to be reclaimed` IS A NUMBER, `wholly within port limits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Approver
`the reclamation must be approved by` MEANS
    IF `hectares to be reclaimed` AT MOST `the ceiling for ministerial authorisation` `wholly within port limits`
    THEN `the Minister`
    ELSE Parliament

§§ `5 -- reclaimed land declared State land`

-- s 5(1): the President may "by proclamation published in the Gazette, declare any lands formed by the reclamation ... to be State
-- land, and thereupon that land shall immediately vest in the State freed and discharged from all public and private rights which
-- may have existed or been claimed over the foreshore or the seabed before the same were so reclaimed." (2): such land "shall be
-- subject to the State Lands Act 1920".
-- Reclamation alone does not extinguish the old rights; the Gazette proclamation does.
GIVEN `the land was formed by reclamation` IS A BOOLEAN, `a proclamation was published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `earlier rights over the foreshore are extinguished` IF
    `the land was formed by reclamation` AND `a proclamation was published in the Gazette`

§§ `6, 7 -- no compensation for the works; appeal to the Minister`

-- s 2: "works" means the works and things mentioned in section 4 (quays, wharves, jetties and other public works, dredging, buildings
-- on reclaimed land).
-- s 6: "Except as provided by this Act, no person shall be entitled to claim, and no action or proceeding shall be brought, against the
-- Government to recover any compensation in respect of any lands ... injuriously affected by the execution of the works."
-- s 7(1): "there shall ... be no right to compensation ... whether on account of loss of sea frontage or for any other reason".
-- (2): "Any person, whose property has been damaged by the execution of the works, may appeal to the Minister, whose decision shall be
-- final." (3): the Minister "may, in his discretion", after inquiry by an appointed officer, (a) authorise payment of "such sum as he
-- may determine" or (b) direct repairs.
--
-- Loss of sea frontage alone is named as giving no right to compensation. Whether it counts as property "damaged" for the s 7(2)
-- appeal is not said; this encoding (an inference) treats the appeal as open only where property was damaged.
DECLARE Harm IS ONE OF
    `loss of sea frontage`
    `loss of a sea view`
    `physical damage to a building`
    `physical damage to a seawall or jetty`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the harm is damage to property` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `physical damage to a building` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `physical damage to a seawall or jetty` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm, `caused by the execution of the works` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a right to compensation from the Government` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the harm` IS A Harm, `caused by the execution of the works` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may appeal to the Minister` IF
    `caused by the execution of the works` AND `the harm is damage to property` `the harm`

DECLARE Outcome IS ONE OF
    `payment of a sum the Minister determines`
    `repairs by the appropriate authority`
    `damages assessed by a court`
    `a further appeal to the courts`

GIVEN `the outcome` IS AN Outcome
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's appeal can lead to` IF
    CONSIDER `the outcome`
    WHEN `payment of a sum the Minister determines` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `repairs by the appropriate authority` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `8 -- validation of grants made before 25 January 1901`

-- s 8: where a lease or grant "was, before 25 January 1901, made by the Governor" of foreshore or seabed within territorial waters,
-- "and before that date the land had been reclaimed or wharves, docks, landing stages or other works or buildings had been erected
-- thereon", the grant "shall be deemed to be a valid conveyance ... free and discharged from all public rights".
-- Both events must precede 25 January 1901. Dates are given as year, month, day.
GIVEN `y` IS A NUMBER, `m` IS A NUMBER, `d` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is before 25 January 1901` IF
        `y` LESS THAN 1901
    OR  (`y` EQUALS 1901 AND `m` EQUALS 1 AND `d` LESS THAN 25)

GIVEN `made by the Governor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `grant year` IS A NUMBER, `grant month` IS A NUMBER, `grant day` IS A NUMBER,
      `works year` IS A NUMBER, `works month` IS A NUMBER, `works day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the old grant is validated` IF
        `made by the Governor`
    AND `is before 25 January 1901` `grant year` `grant month` `grant day`
    AND `is before 25 January 1901` `works year` `works month` `works day`

§§ `9 -- leases of foreshore and seabed`

-- s 9(1): the President "may make such leases ... as are declared by the President not to create a substantial infringement of public
-- rights". (2): the term "shall not exceed 100 years except in special cases". (3): before the declaration, the substance of the lease
-- must be published in the Gazette with a notice requiring objections "in writing to the Minister before the expiration of 3 weeks from
-- the date of the publication", and "all these objections shall be considered by the President".
GIVEN `term in years` IS A NUMBER, `a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease term is permitted` IF
    `term in years` AT MOST 100 OR `a special case`

GIVEN `declared no substantial infringement of public rights` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `gazetted with a call for objections` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `objections considered by the President` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `term in years` IS A NUMBER, `a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the lease may be made` IF
        `declared no substantial infringement of public rights`
    AND `gazetted with a call for objections`
    AND `objections considered by the President`
    AND `the lease term is permitted` `term in years` `a special case`

-- "before the expiration of 3 weeks from the date of the publication": counted here (an inference; the Interpretation Act was not
-- read) as excluding the day of publication, so an objection sent within 21 days after it is in time.
GIVEN `days after publication` IS A NUMBER, `in writing to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the objection is in time` IF
    `days after publication` AT MOST 21 AND `in writing to the Minister`

-- s 9(4): every lease must specify its purposes and contain (a) a proviso that if the lessees fail "at any time during the continuance
-- of the term of the lease to use the demised land for the purposes so specified", a Collector of Land Revenue (or an officer he
-- authorises in writing) "may on behalf of the State re-enter ... and thereupon the same shall be forfeited to and vest in the State";
-- and (b) "a reservation to the State of all mines and minerals under the demised lands".
GIVEN `the term is running` IS A BOOLEAN, `the land is used for the specified purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the State may re-enter and forfeit` IF
    `the term is running` AND (NOT `the land is used for the specified purposes`)

-- s 9(5): "'minerals' includes corals, stone, clay, sand, gravel, and other natural deposits, brine, petroleum and any other mineral oil
-- or relative hydrocarbon, and natural gas." The list is inclusive; only listed items are asserted.
DECLARE Material IS ONE OF
    sand
    coral
    gravel
    stone
    clay
    brine
    petroleum
    `natural gas`

GIVEN `the material` IS A Material
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is reserved to the State` IF
    TRUE

§§ `10 -- temporary occupation licences`

-- s 10(1): licences "for the temporary occupation for any period not exceeding one year of the foreshore and seabed". (2): the power is
-- "exercisable by the Commissioner of Lands or by a Collector of Land Revenue deputed by him in that behalf"; licences follow the State
-- Lands Act 1920 rules for temporary occupation of State land, "Provided that no licence granted under this section shall be renewed
-- if it is made to appear to the Minister that the licence creates a substantial infringement of public rights."
-- Reading s 10(2) as naming the only officers who may grant is an inference from "exercisable by".
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner of Lands`
    `a Collector of Land Revenue deputed by the Commissioner`
    `a Collector of Land Revenue not so deputed`
    `the Minister`

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence may be granted` IF
        `months` AT MOST 12
    AND CONSIDER `the officer`
        WHEN `the Commissioner of Lands` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a Collector of Land Revenue deputed by the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `shown to the Minister to infringe public rights substantially` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence may be renewed` IF
    NOT `shown to the Minister to infringe public rights substantially`

§§ `11 -- farming the use of beaches`

-- s 11(1): the President may "rent or farm ... by public sale or by public tender ... the use of the beaches and banks of the sea",
-- with limits on the farmer's charges. (2): rents due to the Government "shall be recoverable as Government debts". (3): the farmer may
-- sue a tenant or person using the farmed rights for the money payable "as agreed on between the parties". (4): "No such farmer shall
-- recover a larger sum than that specially agreed on between him and the tenant nor a larger sum than that permitted in the grant by
-- the President to be charged by the farmer."
GIVEN `sum agreed with the user` IS A NUMBER, `charge permitted by the grant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the farmer can recover` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `sum agreed with the user` `charge permitted by the grant`

GIVEN `by public sale or public tender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the beach farm is validly let` IF
    `by public sale or public tender`

-- s 12: nothing in the Act derogates from the Government's powers over the foreshore or territorial waters, "nor shall anything in this
-- Act be deemed to affect any right or claim as between lessees and their sublessees or tenants". Not encoded.
